This is a hospital patient vital-signs monitoring system.

STACK:
- Next.js App Router, TypeScript (this repo uses Next.js 16 — use proxy.ts, not middleware.ts)
- Prisma 6 + PostgreSQL (Neon)
- Tailwind CSS
- Deployed on Vercel (Root Directory: patient-monitor if the git repo parent is the workspace)

DEPLOY / DATABASE (Neon + Vercel):
- DATABASE_URL = Neon pooled connection (hostname has -pooler). App runtime uses this.
- DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED = Neon direct connection (no -pooler). Prisma Migrate uses this via directUrl.
- Neon↔Vercel integration injects both names automatically — do not rename them.
- SESSION_SECRET must be set manually in Vercel env vars (and locally in .env).
- Build runs: prisma generate && prisma migrate deploy && next build
- Prefer Prisma Client over raw drivers; keep the singleton in lib/prisma.ts for serverless.
- Do not use Prisma Edge client or @prisma/adapter-neon unless asked — stick to pooled TCP + Prisma 6.

DATA MODEL:
- Ward → Room → Patient → Device → Reading
- Adding a patient requires selecting an existing Room (never assign Patient directly to Ward)
- Reading = heart_rate, spo2, temp_c, systolic, diastolic, recorded_at

ALERT SCORING:
- Use NEWS2-inspired aggregate scoring (lib/vitalScore.ts), not single-value thresholds.
- Label it "NEWS2-inspired" in UI/docs — never claim full NEWS2 compliance
  (missing respiratory rate + consciousness level).
- URGENT if aggregate ≥ 5, LOW if ≥ 1, else NORMAL.

DEVICE INGESTION:
- ESP32 devices POST readings to /api/readings with header x-api-key
- API route must validate api_key against Device table before writing
- Never trust device_id/patient_id from the request body — resolve from api_key server-side
- Device apiKey is shown once at creation (secret), not browsable in plaintext later

DASHBOARD:
- Polling-based updates (fetch every 3-5s), NOT WebSockets
- Routes: /dashboard (wards), /dashboard/wards/[id]/rooms, room patient lists,
  /dashboard/patients/[id], /dashboard/staff (admin)
- Role-based access as below

ROLES:
- admin — full CRUD, all wards; creates all staff accounts; password resets admin-only
- doctor — read all wards; no ward restriction; no ward/room/staff CRUD
- nurse — read/write own ward only
- No self-registration — admin creates accounts via /dashboard/staff
- No self-service password change for this project scope (admin resets via staff tools if needed)

AUTH:
- Custom email+password only. bcrypt for hashing, jose for signed httpOnly session cookies.
- No NextAuth, no OAuth providers, no magic links.
- Protect /dashboard via proxy.ts (Next.js 16); verify the session JWT from the request cookie.

DO NOT:
- Suggest WebSockets or Socket.io
- Suggest multi-tenant subdomain routing (not needed — single hospital, multiple wards)
- Add features not in this spec without asking first
- Claim full NEWS2 compliance
